# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage
test-results/
playwright-report/

# leftover Next.js cache (must not return as a runtime)
/.next/
/out/

# SPA production bundle (spa:build)
/spa/dist


# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem
.commandcode/
.kiro/

# Python bytecode from BMad skill scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
data.db
data.db-*
data.db-wal
data.db-shm
data.db.bak-*

# Local corpus dumps / source decks (not runtime assets)
/*.pptx

# Ephemeral generated PPTX cache (FR-10b)
.cache/

# Hub-local uploads (default UPLOADS_DIR). Sermon graphics are harmless, but the
# same directory holds family- and youth-of-the-week photos of real members —
# runtime data on a durable host path, never repository content.
/data/uploads/

# --- Public repository guard -------------------------------------------------
# This repo is public. A congregation's own data never enters it.
# Private overrides live here and are seeded automatically when present.
data/local/

# Real service exports, member photos and uploaded flyers.
data/uploads/
slides/
slides-all/
slides-new/

# Source presentation decks are extraction inputs, never committed.
*.pptx
*.potx

# Claude Code worktrees. `.worktreeinclude` copies .env, data.db, data/local/
# and data/uploads/ into every new worktree, so these directories hold exactly
# the categories above. Claude Code also excludes this path via
# .git/info/exclude, but that file is per-clone and never shared — the rule has
# to live here to survive a fresh clone or CI.
.claude/worktrees/

# Local databases and their backups.
data/*.db
data.db.bak-*

# Raw diff dumps from review sessions. A diff is worse than scratch output: it
# records the *pre-remediation* state of the files it touches, which is exactly
# what a sanitisation pass removes from the tree. `_bmad-output/review-diff.diff`
# was tracked from the initial commit until 2026-08-01 and the guard never read
# it — `.diff` is absent from TEXT_EXTENSIONS, and PowerShell had written it as
# UTF-16, so the name matcher saw letters separated by NUL. It happened to be
# clean. Not producing the value beats blocking it afterwards.
#
# `*.patch` is deliberately NOT added here: `!.yarn/patches` above un-ignores
# that directory, and a blanket `*.patch` would silently re-ignore its contents.
# Scratch directory images and binary assets (.work is committed scratch, but images must never be tracked outside public/)
.work/**/images/
.work/**/*.png
.work/**/*.jpg
.work/**/*.jpeg

# Go build output
*.exe
/cmd/api/api

*.diff

# Screenshot evidence for WYSIWYG parity analysis. Images may only be tracked
# under public/ (tests/public-repo-guard.test.mjs); these stay local.
.scratch/**/*.png

# Local scratch fonts in .work
.work/*.ttf
